  "title": "Erdős Problem #623",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $X$ be a set of cardinality $\\aleph_\\omega$ and $f$ be a function from the finite subsets of $X$ to $X$ such that $f(A)\not\\in A$ for all $A$. Must there exist an infinite $Y\\subseteq X$ that is independent - that is, for all finite $B\\subset Y$ we have $f(B)\not\\in Y$?",
